        <origin>Anamika Dristi</origin>
        <pubdate>20261024</pubdate>
        <title>CRMS herbaceous marsh vegetation, hydrology, extreme-event exposure and MODIS NDVI by site and year, coastal Louisiana, 2006-2025</title>
        <geoform>tabular digital data</geoform>
        <onlink>https://github.com/anamikadristi/coastal-marsh-vegetation-extreme-events</onlink>
      </citeinfo>
    </citation>
    <descript>
      <abstract>One row per Coastwide Reference Monitoring System (CRMS) herbaceous marsh site and survey year (6439 rows, 341 sites, 2006-2025). Each row combines plot vegetation summaries (total cover, species richness, halophyte cover share, a salinity index from species composition, black mangrove presence) with April-September salinity and flooding from CRMS continuous recorders, MODIS NDVI within 1 km, nClimDiv drought indices, HURDAT2 hurricane exposure and February 2021 freeze minimum temperature. It is an independent derived product built from public data.</abstract>
      <purpose>To study how Louisiana coastal marsh vegetation responds to hurricanes, the February 2021 freeze and the 2022-2023 drought, and how vegetation relates to salinity, flooding and satellite greenness, by marsh type.</purpose>
      <supplinf>Associations only; the dataset supports observational analyses and does not establish causes. Code and documentation: scripts/ and docs/METADATA_NOTES.md in the repository.</supplinf>
    </descript>
