      <procstep>
        <procdesc>Downloaded the public inputs without accounts or keys (scripts/01_download_data.py).</procdesc>
        <procdate>20261024</procdate>
      </procstep>
      <procstep>
        <procdesc>Reduced the hourly CRMS hydrographic export to station-day salinity, water level relative to the marsh surface and flooded fraction, requiring 12 or more valid hours per day (scripts/02_build_hydro_daily.py).</procdesc>
        <procdate>20261024</procdate>
      </procstep>
      <procstep>
        <procdesc>Selected herbaceous marsh plots (Freshwater, Intermediate, Brackish, Saline; years 2006-2025), coded cover classes (&lt;1 as 0.5, Solitary as 0.1) and summarised plots to site-years (scripts/03_vegetation_site_year.py).</procdesc>
        <procdate>20261024</procdate>
      </procstep>
      <procstep>
        <procdesc>Summarised hydrology by site for April-September, requiring 90 or more valid days (scripts/04_hydro_growing_season.py).</procdesc>
        <procdate>20261024</procdate>
      </procstep>
      <procstep>
        <procdesc>Computed hurricane, freeze and drought exposure for each site from HURDAT2, GHCN-Daily and nClimDiv (scripts/05_event_exposure.py).</procdesc>
        <procdate>20261024</procdate>
      </procstep>
      <procstep>
        <procdesc>Read MOD13Q1 NDVI windows at 1 km site buffers from Microsoft Planetary Computer and kept good or marginal pixels (scripts/06_modis_ndvi.py).</procdesc>
        <procdate>20261024</procdate>
      </procstep>
      <procstep>
        <procdesc>Joined all inputs, derived the baseline marsh type, salinity index and growing-season NDVI, and wrote the site-year CSV (scripts/07_build_site_year_dataset.py).</procdesc>
        <procdate>20261024</procdate>
      </procstep>
